{
  "title": "Waar ben je heen gegaan?",
  "goal": "Talk about a journey or a change of place with zijn and a past participle.",
  "imageIdeas": [
    {
      "afterHeading": "Story: catching up again",
      "description": "Sofia and Noor talk at the kitchen table in Sofia's Utrecht apartment, with a simple map of Utrecht nearby.",
      "alt": "Sofia tells Noor about her return to Utrecht and a walk in the city."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "content": "Waar ben je heen gegaan?",
      "id": "7d985d6c-15b5-4215-abff-ce0551cf9f98"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "It is Tuesday 5 January 2027. Sofia and Noor continue their holiday catch-up. Sofia tells Noor about returning to Utrecht and taking a short walk in the city. In this lesson you will use zijn with a past participle for a small set of movement and change verbs.",
      "id": "c3b5310d-4763-40fc-9d3a-15e2bf700022"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Colours: finite verbs are blue, subjects are green, places are purple, and the new participles are bold.",
      "id": "60798312-a459-4d1e-8fbe-92f3d77ddb91"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Story: catching up again",
      "id": "f8715a9d-caa0-4270-8e64-96491bc08b08"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Hoi Sofia! Hoe gaat het?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Goed, dank je. Ik ben weer terug in Utrecht."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Fijn! Ben je zondag aangekomen?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, ik ben zondag teruggekomen."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "En gisteren? Ben je thuisgebleven?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Nee, ik ben naar het centrum gegaan."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Ben je ook naar het park gegaan?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, en daarna ben ik naar huis gegaan."
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "1fa1ee41-5c92-4c5c-99a3-7775bdd2b8d7"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "grammar",
        "icon": "book-open"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "For this lesson's selected movement and change verbs, use ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "text": "zijn + past participle",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true,
            "textColor": "blue"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". The finite form of zijn changes; the participle goes at the end: Sofia is naar huis gegaan.",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "id": "3ebe42f7-18c2-487a-a2e8-d97a50f724d5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "A small set of verbs with zijn",
      "id": "42ea54e1-baba-4deb-ba3c-347a2cc6bb78"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You already know how a participle sits at the end from row 25. Here, learn these complete verb forms as useful chunks. The lesson does not explain how irregular participles are made.",
      "id": "322e0783-7667-4d90-b9ed-67aa636b780c"
    },
