      "content": "A short walk in Utrecht",
      "id": "6e7c6ada-0750-4bf3-a129-c347e646f54c"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "On Monday 4 January, Sofia went for a short walk in the city. These examples use familiar places and past participles as whole forms.",
      "id": "8fdcf3e8-51a5-4920-9a3c-597c64da70b8"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "Ik ben naar het centrum ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "text": "gegaan",
          "styles": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "props": {
        "translation": "I went to the city centre.",
        "note": "Destination follows naar; gegaan is at the end."
      },
      "id": "8c210185-f548-4258-bd91-3ff88499085c"
    },
