        "note": "This does not state how she travelled."
      },
      "id": "0fc4ac3e-a7fc-407f-b3a9-85c0c238a5c8"
    },
    {
      "type": "bulletListItem",
      "content": "Remember the complete forms:",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "gaan → gegaan; komen → gekomen",
          "id": "f866fdc4-dfb8-4b89-9bc7-5a107e837121"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "aankomen → aangekomen; terugkomen → teruggekomen",
          "id": "984a8f0f-bf8c-4bbd-88cc-25739f00f768"
        },
        {
          "type": "bulletListItem",
          "content": "vertrekken → vertrokken; blijven → gebleven",
          "id": "f0176b46-4dd4-487e-863e-8d28fd81db94"
        }
      ],
      "id": "6c01091f-d252-4e4b-b4aa-8cb5085abcad"
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "variant": "hint",
        "icon": "lightbulb"
      },
      "content": "Learn the six infinitive–participle pairs as complete chunks. Row 27 will explain how these participle forms are built.",
      "id": "9f626cdf-1c59-4df9-ab12-c09d0aa78d87"
    },
    {
      "type": "dialogue",
      "props": {
        "turns": [
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Gisteren ben ik naar het centrum gegaan."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Ben je ook naar de gracht gegaan?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ja, ik ben langs de gracht gegaan."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "We zijn met de trein naar Zandvoort gegaan."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Ben je daar met Daan en mij naartoe gegaan?"
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Ja, ik ben met jullie naar Zandvoort gegaan."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Sofia",
            "text": "Daar zijn we in een strandcafé gebleven."
          },
          {
            "speaker": "Noor",
            "text": "Wat gezellig!"
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "838c88f5-e1d1-4f84-82bd-9d0f31bfb35e"
    },
    {
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "words": [
            {
              "term": "langs de gracht",
              "meaning": "along the canal",
              "example": "Ik ben langs de gracht gegaan.",
              "id": "a4a64798-a705-4451-a92d-1e0fc80eca47"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "b9fbb15a-ae65-4867-9bbb-e645c2dbc683"
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "id": "fd6da697-0f01-4ba6-b580-73f7860926a7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Practice",
      "id": "a194c601-abd3-4720-9923-cb0d94a626d5"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "1. Choose the right form",
      "id": "1bebff81-9826-48a6-bd6f-074fa33b2cf2"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Complete each sentence with the correct form of zijn and the participle in brackets.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia … zondag in Utrecht … . (aankomen)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "is",
                "aangekomen"
              ],
              "note": "Sofia takes is; put the participle at the end."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wij … naar huis … . (gaan)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "zijn",
                "gegaan"
              ],
              "note": "Wij takes zijn; the destination comes before the participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wij … thuis … . (blijven)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "zijn",
                "gebleven"
              ],
              "note": "Wij takes zijn; learn gebleven as a whole form."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Daan … vroeg … . (vertrekken)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "is",
                "vertrokken"
              ],
              "note": "Daan takes is; vertrokken is the selected participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Ik … gisteren … . (terugkomen)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "ben",
                "teruggekomen"
              ],
              "note": "Ik takes ben; teruggekomen stays at the end."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Jullie … samen … . (komen)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "zijn",
                "gekomen"
              ],
              "note": "Jullie takes zijn."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "De trein … om acht uur … . (vertrekken)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "is",
                "vertrokken"
              ],
              "note": "A singular subject takes is."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "b6409428-3257-405a-9df5-ae451ad3d842"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "2. Recall the participle",
      "id": "15cf1322-3817-4942-8850-ec07c8ebaa6e"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Write the past participle. Learn these forms as complete words.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "gaan → …",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gegaan"
              ],
              "note": "This irregular form is introduced as a whole; its pattern is for row 27."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "komen → …",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gekomen"
              ],
              "note": "This irregular form is introduced as a whole; its pattern is for row 27."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "aankomen → …",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "aangekomen"
              ],
              "note": "Keep aan together at the beginning of this participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "terugkomen → …",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "teruggekomen"
              ],
              "note": "Keep terug together at the beginning of this participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "vertrekken → …",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "vertrokken"
              ],
              "note": "Learn vertrokken as a complete form."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "blijven → …",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gebleven"
              ],
              "note": "Learn gebleven as a complete form."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Fill in: Ik ben naar huis … . (gaan)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "gegaan"
              ],
              "note": "The participle closes the sentence."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "120cc613-c4fc-462b-a6a4-1e346f9d529a"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "3. Complete the conversation",
      "id": "58fcd4af-9bbd-43cd-a3e1-364cc882e600"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Complete Noor and Sofia's chat with the right form.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Noor: … je zondag …? (aankomen)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ben",
                "aangekomen"
              ],
              "note": "Start a yes/no question with ben."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia: Ja, ik … zondag … . (terugkomen)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "ben",
                "teruggekomen"
              ],
              "note": "Ik takes ben; the participle goes last."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor: … je gisteren naar het centrum …? (gaan)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ben",
                "gegaan"
              ],
              "note": "Put finite ben first in the question."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia: Ja, ik … naar het centrum … . (gaan)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "ben",
                "gegaan"
              ],
              "note": "The destination comes before gegaan."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor: Ik … thuis … . (blijven)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "ben",
                "gebleven"
              ],
              "note": "Ik takes ben; gebleven ends the sentence."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia: … Daan al …? (vertrekken)",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Is",
                "vertrokken"
              ],
              "note": "Daan is singular, so the question begins with is."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "f8173fff-42be-4fbe-a865-3fe6df26d13a"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "4. Put the participle last",
      "id": "522e2072-9244-409c-8d4b-0f398097d171"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Put the chunks in order. Write a complete sentence.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "gisteren / ik / ben / naar huis / gegaan",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Gisteren ben ik naar huis gegaan."
              ],
              "note": "A fronted time word is followed by the finite verb, then the subject; the participle is last."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "is / Sofia / zondag / aangekomen / in Utrecht",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Sofia is zondag in Utrecht aangekomen."
              ],
              "note": "Use subject + finite verb + other information + participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "ben / je / naar het centrum / gegaan",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ben je naar het centrum gegaan?"
              ],
              "note": "A yes/no question starts with ben."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "thuis / zijn / Noor en Fleur / gebleven",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Noor en Fleur zijn thuisgebleven."
              ],
              "note": "The compound thuisgebleven is written as one word."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "om acht uur / de trein / is / vertrokken",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "De trein is om acht uur vertrokken."
              ],
              "note": "Place the participle at the end."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "samen / zijn / wij / teruggekomen",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Wij zijn samen teruggekomen."
              ],
              "note": "Subject + zijn + other information + participle."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "59172432-0846-450e-91dc-a7f1bf949a1d"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "5. Change present to perfect",
      "id": "adbf92d6-7699-442e-8da7-44df3870f4ef"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Rewrite each sentence in the perfect. Keep the meaning and use zijn.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Ik ga naar huis.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik ben naar huis gegaan."
              ],
              "note": "In this selected set, gaan uses zijn; put gegaan at the end."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Noor komt naar het centrum.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Noor is naar het centrum gekomen."
              ],
              "note": "Noor takes is; gekomen is the participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia komt terug naar Utrecht.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Sofia is naar Utrecht teruggekomen."
              ],
              "note": "The participle goes at the end. Also fine: Sofia is teruggekomen in Utrecht."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Daan vertrekt vroeg.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Daan is vroeg vertrokken."
              ],
              "note": "Use is for singular Daan."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wij blijven thuis.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Wij zijn thuisgebleven."
              ],
              "note": "Wij takes zijn; thuisgebleven is one word."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Jullie komen zondag aan.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Jullie zijn zondag aangekomen."
              ],
              "note": "Jullie takes zijn; aangekomen ends the sentence."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "97e75315-2d1a-452e-9d9a-47e8d423001a"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "content": "6. Translate",
      "id": "a215253f-d36c-4baf-9ded-e79cb289f7cc"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Translate into Dutch or English.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "I arrived in Utrecht on Sunday.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik ben zondag in Utrecht aangekomen."
              ],
              "note": "Do not add a way of travelling; the story does not establish one."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "I stayed at home yesterday.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ik ben gisteren thuisgebleven."
              ],
              "note": "Ik takes ben; use thuisgebleven as one word."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Did you go to the city centre?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ben je naar het centrum gegaan?"
              ],
              "note": "The question starts with ben."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "We came back together.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "We zijn samen teruggekomen."
              ],
              "note": "We and wij both take zijn."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Daan left early.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Daan is vroeg vertrokken."
              ],
              "note": "Vertrokken is the participle of vertrekken."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Sofia is naar huis gegaan.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Sofia went home."
              ],
              "note": "Naar huis names the destination; gegaan is the participle."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Ik ben naar het centrum gegaan.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "I went to the city centre."
              ],
              "note": "Gaan is one of this lesson's selected verbs with zijn."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "5cfce7bd-8655-4210-af14-e6be9a9a3f0c"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Reading: Sofia's return and walk",
      "id": "9c0e64dd-25cb-494d-b9b0-5b2daad623f8"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Read the passage and answer in Dutch.",
          "passage": {
            "title": "Sofia vertelt over zondag en maandag",
            "content": "Op dinsdag praat Sofia met Noor. Sofia is zondag 3 januari naar Utrecht teruggekomen. Ze zegt niets over haar reis. Op maandag is Sofia naar het centrum gegaan. Ze is door het park gegaan en daarna naar huis gegaan. Noor is eerder met Sofia en Daan naar Zandvoort gegaan. Sofia is blij met haar eigen huis en praat met Noor over de wandeling."
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Wanneer is Sofia teruggekomen in Utrecht?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Op zondag 3 januari."
              ],
              "note": "Read the first two sentences; do not guess her transport."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Waar is Sofia op maandag naartoe gegaan?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Naar het centrum."
              ],
              "note": "The destination is naar het centrum."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Is Sofia door het park gegaan?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ja, Sofia is door het park gegaan."
              ],
              "note": "The passage says she went through the park."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Waar is Sofia daarna naartoe gegaan?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Naar huis."
              ],
              "note": "Daarna is ze naar huis gegaan."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Is Noor met Sofia en Daan naar Zandvoort gegaan?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ja, Noor is met Sofia en Daan naar Zandvoort gegaan."
              ],
              "note": "The passage retells their established trip to Zandvoort."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Met wie praat Sofia op dinsdag?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Met Noor."
              ],
              "note": "Sofia praat met Noor."
            },
            {
              "prompt": "Wat zegt de tekst over Sofia's reis?",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Ze zegt niets over haar reis."
              ],
              "note": "The passage deliberately leaves the travel mode unspecified."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "9c3a7878-41ec-4e07-ab8a-889e06071410"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Your turn",
      "id": "cfad500c-d416-440f-8016-656906a388dd"
    },
    {
      "type": "practice",
      "props": {
        "data": {
          "instruction": "Write two or three Dutch sentences about a journey or movement. Use at least one form of zijn and a participle from this lesson.",
          "items": [
            {
              "prompt": "Tell a friend where you went or whether you stayed at home. Include a time or place.",
              "authorsVersion": [
                "Gisteren ben ik naar het park gegaan. Daarna ben ik naar huis gegaan."
              ],
              "note": "Answers vary. Keep the participle at the end of each sentence; also fine: Ik ben thuisgebleven."
            }
          ]
        }
