      "id": "8467b1be-4b74-4c04-82e9-9bd1fcbae010"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": "Summary",
      "id": "e4a581ce-ccdd-4850-84e8-424053a0b10e"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "For this lesson's selected movement and change verbs, use a form of zijn plus the participle.",
      "id": "41000613-48ea-4452-8a38-9f043c87817f"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "In statements, put the participle at the end. In yes/no questions, put ben/is/zijn first.",
      "id": "08d3344a-182d-4c1a-8d15-455cc0c5d943"
    },
    {
      "type": "numberedListItem",
      "content": "Learn gegaan, gekomen, aangekomen, teruggekomen, vertrokken and gebleven as whole forms; row 27 explains participle patterns.",
      "id": "9b430f12-8f2e-454a-9057-db95a7e46859"
    }
  ],
  "id": "6f360b93-0a7b-46a2-ba35-b958dfe907f0"
